WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.036
As soon as one artillery round

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:06.172
blasts toward Bakhmut,

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.742
the crew rushes to prepare for another

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.877
Ukrainian officials report

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.445
gains in the town.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.913
That since last year has been

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:17.150
the epicenter of the war.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.518
Gun Commander

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:21.054
Artem has been in the area for months,

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.090
reaching the task of taking down

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.859
coordinates and barking orders.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:27.060
Now, routine

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.061
He says he's now

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:31.164
half deaf from the blast.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.500
Yet he has sense to change.

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:37.170
It seems like they're often running away,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.205
he says, referring to the Russians.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:43.009
And then the order to fire

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.013
There's barely

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.416
a let up in the distant third shelling

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.018
target.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:52.519
The Russian

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.287
says this gunner call sign

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.289
Aries are falling back.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:58.792
We know because they hit us, much less.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.193
One or two months ago,

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:01.861
there was a lot of incoming.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.463
It was scary to be here.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:04.431
Now it's different

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:08.735
On another flank, the big guns are out.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.603
This is a book, Dana.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:13.573
A Ukrainian made 155 millimeters

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:16.576
self-propelled Howitzer

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.446
Ukraine claims the Russians have poured

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:22.615
as many as 50,000 troops into the defense

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.718
of the town, dug in deep Russian.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.120
It was only the Russians

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.621
who fortified their positions

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.123
and stand strong, Commander

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.524
Dmitry tells me.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:34.561
But I think that's temporary.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.463
Russian soldiers captured in the battle

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.263
here told us

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.965
the shelling on their positions

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.367
was relentless warfare.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:43.603
That was a

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.940
high explosive anti-personnel munition

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:50.110
fired at the direction of Russian troops

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.846
outside of Bakhmut.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.315
As soon as they fired,

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:57.317
they prepare to fire again.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.455
Now, it appears that the Ukrainians

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.690
are really pulling out

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.925
all the stops around Bakhmut.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:06.993
Over the months,

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.428
I've been covering the battle

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.130
in and around that town.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.031
I've always heard the Ukrainians complain

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.900
about a shortage of ammunition.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.902
We didn't hear that today.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.770
They seem to have more than enough.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.639
One of those batteries told us

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.574
that they're firing

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:25.411
50, 6100 rounds a day.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.913
It really does appear

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.048
that Bakhmut is at the moment

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:31.284
the focus of this Ukrainian

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.919
counter-offensive Wolf.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:33.820
Very interesting.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.221
Ben Wedeman, stay safe over there.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.389
Thank you very much.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.123
Right now,

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:37.991
let's bring in

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:40.126
CNN contributor on Russian affairs,

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:42.262
Jill Dougherty and CNN military analyst

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.430
retired Colonel Cedric Leighton.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.064
Colonel Leighton,

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.100
now that Ukraine will be receiving

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.202
these u.s.-made cluster bombs

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.271
How will they leverage those weapons

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:53.640
in their counter offensive right now

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.676
while limiting Syria's collateral damage?

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.144
You can see in this video

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:00.613
of a Russian attack on Kharkiv.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.015
The bombs don't always

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:03.383
detonate immediately

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:06.286
Yeah, that's going to be a

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.221
big challenge for them both.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:09.722
But the basic premise

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.024
behind the Ukrainian effort

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.659
to get cluster munitions

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:13.626
is that they will use them

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:15.328
against the trenches that the Russians

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.262
have drawn up

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.864
all throughout the eastern front

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:19.566
as well as the southern front.

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:20.600
So if they do that

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.768
and if they limit

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:22.802
the target area

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.404
of those cluster munitions,

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.072
they might be able to limit

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.907
the civilian exposure to them once

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.742
this war is over.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.744
Jill, you're an expert on Russia.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.146
We know Russia has been using

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.314
these cluster bombs

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:36.549
against Ukrainians for some time.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.018
How are they reacting to this news

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.987
that the US is about to provide

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:42.355
these cluster munitions

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.490
to the Ukrainians?

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:45.358
You know, Wolf,

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.227
I've been looking at several stories

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:51.064
in the Russian media and every single one

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.233
immediately jumps on the admission

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.201
by the Biden administration

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.703
that these weapons are,

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.837
you know, dangerous

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.572
for civilians, civilians,

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.207
or at least they can be.

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:03.576
And then also, I think significantly

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:04.310
they're saying,

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.446
hey, look, the United States and Ukraine

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:07.547
never signed

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.515
the international conventions

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.952
about these weapons, ignoring the fact

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.454
and not including the fact

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:16.456
that Russia hasn't either.

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:18.224
And then again,

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:18.891
noting that

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:21.194
the Ukrainians are using these weapons,

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:24.664
this ammunition in Ukraine right now,

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.700
leaving out the fact that Russia is so

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.003
what they're doing is it's obviously part

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.704
of the propaganda approach

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.439
and just trying to take advantage of it

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:36.509
and make the United States look very bad

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:38.011
for making that decision.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:41.080
And Jill, let me follow up.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:41.514
The U.S.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.416
says the NATO members

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.917
who will be meeting next week

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.653
at the summit in Lithuania

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:48.888
will not admit Ukraine to the alliance,

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.523
at least not yet.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.392
But how much does any progress toward

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:55.361
that goal actually feed Putin's anxiety

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.298
Well,

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:01.234
he obviously does not want any expansion

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.602
of NATO whatsoever.

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:03.202
But I think what

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.871
the Russians are trying to do

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:08.741
is exploit any division among the allies

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:10.009
or between the allies.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:11.778
So this issue of,

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:14.314
you know, should Sweden join?

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.449
Obviously, Finland already is.

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.451
But Sweden is a big issue.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.853
And because there are differences

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:23.056
in terms of Ukraine,

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:24.190
whether Ukraine should

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.625
ultimately be given

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:28.027
any type of promise or indication

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:29.862
that it could be a member,

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.464
that's where the Russians

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.333
are going to try to exploit

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:36.269
as much as possible any type of division.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.271
So what Naito is trying to do,

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:39.872
obviously, is figure out

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:42.375
how it can give security guarantees

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:44.377
to Ukraine, which are crucial,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.946
and then how they can present

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:48.548
something to Ukraine

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:49.782
that would be forward

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:52.652
looking in terms of possible membership.

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:54.120
You know, it's interesting,

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:54.987
Colonel Leighton,

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:57.090
the NATO's summit will also focus,

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.791
we're told, on long term

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:00.960
security assistance for Ukraine,

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.396
including F-16 fighter jets.

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:05.798
What should be prioritized right now

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:07.033
based on what you know

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.935
about Ukraine's capabilities,

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:10.203
at least at this moment?

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.139
Well, I think, Wolf, one of the key

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:14.741
things is watching

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:15.641
the military speak

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.243
is called interoperability.

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:18.444
And that is the idea

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.313
that Ukrainian systems

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:23.116
should be able to talk to NATO's

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:24.250
weapons systems.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:27.253
So anything that they can be made to work

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.721
together in the sense

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:30.423
that in a doctrinal sense,

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:32.492
that is exactly what the NATO's

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:35.962
meeting should actually result in.

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:38.331
And if they can do that with F-16s,

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:39.532
that will allow

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:41.267
a great deal of interoperability

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:42.935
between the Ukrainian Air Force

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:44.771
and NATO's air forces.

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:45.805
That would be one

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:46.873
step in that direction

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:49.008
and also long range weapons

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:50.543
that could be interoperable

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:51.878
between those areas.

00:06:51.878 --> 00:06:53.079
That would be another

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:55.148
plus for the Ukrainians.

00:06:55.148 --> 00:06:56.482
Colonel Leighton and Jill Dougherty,

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:57.750
guys, thank you very much.

